      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given: The least common multiple (LCM) of two integers is 36 and their greatest common divisor (GCD) is 6. We need to find the product of these two numbers.\n\nLet the two integers be \\( a \\) and \\( b \\). Let the LCM be \\( \\text{LCM}(a, b) = 36 \\) and the GCD be \\( \\text{GCD}(a, b) = 6 \\).\n\nAccording to the properties of LCM and GCD, we know:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nCalculate the product:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = 216\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of the two numbers is \\(\\boxed{216}\\).",
