      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we start by defining the two integers as \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). We know the following:\n\n1. The greatest common divisor (gcd) of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 6.\n2. The least common multiple (lcm) of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 36.\n\nBy the relationship between the gcd and lcm of two numbers, we have:\n\\[\n\\text{gcd}(a, b) \\times \\text{lcm}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\nSubstituting the given values, we get:\n\\[\n6 \\times 36 = a \\times b\n\\]\nSimplifying the left side, we have:\n\\[\n216 = a \\times b\n\\]\nThus, the product of the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
